name issue_15_aimd_v2_cross_traffic
describe A 1.5 Mbps competing flow joins a 3 Mbps bottleneck at 10 s and leaves at 25 s, `cc v2` (#15)
# Utilization: `cc v1` 64-69 %, `cc v2` 71-79 %, libwebrtc 74.2 % (parity-data, 10 seeds). Queue p95 stays
# under the suite's limit (v2 79-171 ms; libwebrtc 264 ms).
cc v2
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=3000kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=1500kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
# Port (#150, RobustThroughputEstimator as the acked-rate estimator, as libwebrtc M157): queue p95 121 -> 262 ms (libwebrtc 263.5,
# per seed 229-292 against ours 204-296), freezes 0 -> 5.2 (libwebrtc 3.9; the same seeds freeze on both stacks: ours
# 2/0/15/0/0/19/0/0/0/16, libwebrtc 2/1/11/1/0/16/1/5/1/1), utilization 73.6 % (libwebrtc 74.2). libwebrtc fails both old lines
# (queue 263.5 > 250, 3.9 freezes), so they move to the level reached on seed 1 (program.md 0.2); needs-human.
expect video.freeze_count <= 2
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 300
expect cc.unsettled == 0
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 68
